{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T015036Z_dev-03_flat_4445", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for ψψ̄ → h2h2 (pure pseudoscalar coupling) used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. The annihilation cross section was ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹, with relic density Ωh² = 0.121. The fit needed the canonical J-factor rescaled by 𝒥 = 2.2, so J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical. The fit gave χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7"}]}, "turns": 8, "seconds": 23.308, "tool_calls": 8, "tool_result_chars": 398672, "input_tokens": 982301, "output_tokens": 1144, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T01:50:59+00:00"}
